## Overview

This project transforms a messy project register (239 projects) into an executive-ready dashboard tracking portfolio health, schedule performance, and budget efficiency. The entire stack is free-tier Google Workspace — no external DB, no paid BI tool.

**Stack:**
- **Google Sheets** — raw data store + cleaned output
- **Google Apps Script** — ETL + KPI calculation
- **Looker Studio (formerly Data Studio)** — visualization layer

---

## Why I Built This

Most PMO reporting lives in stale spreadsheets that nobody updates and nobody trusts. I wanted to prove that with ~80 lines of Apps Script you can:

- Standardize a raw project export into a consistent schema
- Calculate real schedule-performance metrics (SPI, time elapsed, drift status) on the fly
- Backfill missing fields (e.g., Project Manager) without breaking the pipeline
- Pipe it straight into Looker Studio so leadership sees the same numbers the PMs do

The goal: one source of truth, refreshable on demand, viewable on any device.

---

## What the Dashboard Shows

**Summary KPIs**
- Total Projects: `239`
- Portfolio Health: `72.38%`
- Average CPI (Cost Performance Index): `1.29`
- Budget Deviation: `16.74%`

**Visualizations**
- **Project Health Donut** — Green (Healthy) / Yellow (At Risk) / Red (Critical) split
- **Top 5 High-Risk Projects** — table with project name, risk level, budget spent, efficiency
- **Complete % vs. Budget Spent %** — bar chart comparing scheduled progress to actual spend per project

A detailed second page contains the full data dump for drill-down.

